{"authored" [{"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-3i-23j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-23,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-23)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{554}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628" "basis" 1407 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040128/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-316355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $p=⟨0,5,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\times q & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 6)j+(0\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 6)k \\\\  & =5i-6j-30k \\\\  & =⟨5,-6,-30⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,p\\times q\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-30)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36+900} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{961} \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{31}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{31}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-3,5,0⟩$ and $b=⟨4,-1,2⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))i-((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =10i+6j-17k \\\\  & =⟨10,6,-17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-17)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+36+289} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{425} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316345" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316345" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{17}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $f=⟨1,1,-2⟩$ and $g=⟨3,2,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\times g & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))j+(1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =5i-7j-k \\\\  & =⟨5,-7,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,f\\times g\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "5\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19997" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨1,3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-8i+10j-11k \\\\  & =⟨-8,10,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{10}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{285}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{273}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{582}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{825}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{177}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-19983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $h=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $l=⟨4,1,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h\\times l & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 3)i-(2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 3)j+(2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+6j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,h\\times l\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-20004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(1,0,-1)$, $M(3,2,0)$, $N(0,1,3).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i-k) \\\\  & =2i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(j+3k)-(i-k) \\\\  & =-i+j+4k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 1)j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =7i-9j+4k \\\\  & =⟨7,-9,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316516" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316516" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(2,6,6),$ $Q(4,8,2),$ $R(0,5,6).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i+8j+2k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(5j+6k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =-2i-j \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-4))i-(2\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-4))j+(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{21}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{17}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{17}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{21}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-127908" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{21}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY$, if $W(2,-3,1)$, $X(-2,1,2)$, $Y(3,-1,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(-2i+j+2k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =-4i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2)i-((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =6i+9j-12k \\\\  & =⟨6,9,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{97}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{261}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71106" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-1,2,0)$, $E(2,0,1)$, $F(1,3,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =(2i+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(i+3j+2k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)j+(3\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-5i-4j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{90} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DEF$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316514" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316514" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,FGH$, if $F(1,1,2)$, $G(2,2,3)$, $H(1,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =g-f \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =h-f \\\\  & =(i+k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,FGH$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71109" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $VL$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(1,0,1)$, $U(3,2,-1)$, $V(-1,1,0).$\n\n$VL=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $VL$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VL,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =(3i+2j-k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(-i+j)-(i+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =0i+6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =VL\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ VL & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ VL & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $TK$ of the $△\\,RST,$ if $R(4,5,6),$ $S(7,4,5),$ $T(6,8,4).$\n\n$TK=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $TK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,RST$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS\n$$\n\nSo, to find $TK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =s-r \\\\  & =(7i+4j+5k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =3i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =t-r \\\\  & =(6i+8j+4k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)i-(3(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(3\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =5i+4j+11k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{11}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{162} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,RST$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $RS$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RS & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316558" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316558" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $NP$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(3,-1,0)$, $M(0,2,1)$, $N(-2,1,-1).$\n\n$NP=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $NP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $NP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j+k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(-2i+j-k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-5i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-5,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-5))j+((-3)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5))k \\\\  & =-5i-8j+9k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-8,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{170}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LM & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ \\sqrt{170} & =NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ NP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-316392" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-316392" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(4,-1,1),$ $B(0,-3,4),$ $C(2,1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)i-((-4)\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 3)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-12i+6j-12k \\\\  & =⟨-12,6,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 9 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ 18 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{18\\sqrt{10}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}"] ["math" "\\frac{6\\sqrt{33}}{11}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\sqrt{10}}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-128006" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $VH$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(3,2,3)$, $U(0,1,0)$, $V(2,1,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $VH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =j-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-3i-j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(2i+j+2k)-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bbcabdbb2f8a9726e50bfe4a5bff1b10ea888d81dd5535c0ae14913b4036dfa8"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{38}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{19}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{19}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "q-71115" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fb01286887ecddbfe74928be059cafe1514bc2fa55f8bf1dd8e2a6e7516e52e"} {"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 4,0,-3 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 5,-1,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6"} {"question" "e-4344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-3i-23j-4k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-23,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-23)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{554}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\nA_{\\triangle} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{554}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4344.json" "file_sha256" "be9008b647fd975f0099709ab678151b9570bab88495c7fa68dda2e47757c9b6"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940"} {"question" "e-4345" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4345.json" "file_sha256" "a33c2cad52e68b011a7557bbcaa2f942ee343142be1c6db3a33b33cd444e1940"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628"} {"question" "e-4346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040344/example-4346.json" "file_sha256" "af85e9f2cfdc83e3602101d55054860ea26b0101970f16ce6c7d278441a8c628"}] "usage" {"e-4345" [] "e-4346" [] "q-19983" [] "e-4344" []} "basis" 1432 "retractions" [[17592186106045 :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle span